from pathlib import Path
import json
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
states=json.loads((HERE/'states.json').read_text())['states'];exact=json.loads((HERE/'exact-lower-states.json').read_text())
rows=[]
for n in range(2,43):
 top=max(s['achievedOrder'] for s in states if s['n']==n)
 best=next(s for s in states if s['n']==n and s['achievedOrder']==top)
 rows.append(f'<tr><th scope="row">{n}</th><td>{top}</td><td>{best["verification"]["maximumResidual"]}</td></tr>')
(HERE/'index.html').write_text('''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>ACstates library · Verified import through N=42</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css"><style>main{max-width:1000px;padding-block:40px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,48px)}h2{margin-block:28px 14px}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}th,td{padding:9px 16px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}td:last-child{font:12px monospace;max-width:500px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.downloads{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:18px;margin-block:25px}</style></head><body><main><a href="../../index.html">← AC-state catalogue</a><p class="eyebrow">Original library · Import and verification</p><h1>Every qubit number through N=42</h1><p>The catalogue now includes every row from N=1 to N=42, with orders 1–12. Numerical library states are shown in blue; exact constructions and proved exclusions remain distinct. An unfilled higher-order cell records missing evidence rather than a failed-search exclusion.</p><h2>Numerical library representatives</h2><p>87 saved library representatives through N=42 were imported from the audited refinement of the original ACstates folder. Their reported orders were independently checked from the saved 85-digit Dicke components using 100-digit partial traces. Every reported order has Frobenius residual below 10⁻⁶⁰; every next order has residual above 0.00177. These are numerical checks, not exact existence or maximum-order proofs.</p><p>The original coordinate and Dicke files disagree in 16 records across the full library. The catalogue follows the audited coordinate-derived representatives and their refinements, rather than substituting an inconsistent raw Dicke file. Original files and the refinement audit remain linked in the <a href="../../../majorana-degeneracy-catalogue/index.html">Majorana-degeneracy catalogue</a>.</p><p>Two unlisted candidates, acs.29.6_*.txt and acs.13.3.4.txt, fail their claimed orders and are not counted as witnesses. The older acs.37.6.txt state passes; it was independently refined and added as a matching sixth-order representative.</p><h2>Exact lower-order examples</h2><p>'''+str(len(exact['states']))+''' additional analytical states were constructed to match the selected lower order exactly. Normalization, all required reductions and failure at the next order are checked with exact symbolic arithmetic. Together with existing representatives, these provide exact-order defaults whenever available. Where no matching-order construction is recorded, a higher-order representative is labelled by its own order.</p><div class="downloads"><a href="states.json">Saved numerical components ↓</a><a href="verification.json">100-digit verification report ↓</a><a href="verify_numeric.py">Independent numerical verifier ↓</a><a href="exact-lower-states.json">New exact examples ↓</a><a href="verify_exact.py">Independent exact verifier ↓</a><a href="rejected-n29-t6.json">N=29 rejected candidate ↓</a><a href="additional-source-audit.json">Additional source checks ↓</a><a href="extra-state.json">N=37 refinement audit ↓</a></div><h2>Highest order observed in the imported library</h2><p>This column reports the highest audited numerical order available at each size. It does not claim a proved maximum.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">N</th><th scope="col">Reported order</th><th scope="col">Largest residual through that order</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+''.join(rows)+'''</tbody></table></div></main></body></html>''')
